<title>USA: AMBAC qualifies nine issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>AMBAC qualifies nine issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMBAC Indemnity Corp. said Tuesday it qualified for bond insurance the following nine municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Martin County, Fla., $7.7 million General Obligations (GOs).</p>
<p>--Washington Township, Ind., $3.81 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Cheboygan, Mich., $3 million water and sewer GOs.</p>
<p>--Carson City, Nev., $2.94 million refunding GOs.</p>
<p>--Carson City, Nev., $15 million public safty GOs.</p>
<p>--Nichols Hill, Okla., $1.665 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Salem, Ore., $18.54 million revenue bonds.</p>
<p>--Lookout Mountain, Tenn., $1.8 million school GOs.</p>
<p>--Harris County MUD No.222, Texas, $1.96 million unlimited tax. --U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
